findings.comment:
750.800b - The following food contact surfaces were soiled:
A) inside ice machine - white baffle (mold);
B) cleaver left on a metal cart on the make line overnight (food debris) - taken to dish area during inspection;  
C) pot under dry storage shelving (food/general debris) - taken to dish area during inspection;   and
D) baking sheets on bakers rack by the walkin freezer (food debris/grease).

Clean and sanitize food contact surfaces between uses/as needed to prevent cross contamination and eliminate buildup of debris.

750.800e - The following non-food contact surfaces were soiled:
A) (R) shelving in walkin cooler (mold/splash);
B) (R) shelving in dry storage area with bulk powder bins (powder/general buildup);
C) (R) hood filters (grease - especially over the wok area); 
D) (R)  red, black, and green inverted crates used for storage (general buildup); 
E) metal cart between prep coolers on the cook line;
F) floor fan at end of cook line by back door (dust/debris);
G) bulk powder bins (general buildup - outer surfaces);
H) bakers rack by walkin freezer (splash/debris);
I) can opener holder (greasy buildup/metal shavings);   and
J) handles of all coolers (general buildup);

Clean non-food contact surfaces daily/as needed to eliminate buildup of debris.

findings.citation_text:
750.1220 - Floors were soiled with food and/or general debris in the following areas:
A) (R) under ice machine;
B) (R) walkin cooler - along walls/in corners under shelving under shelving/along walls; 
C) SMOOTHIE BAR - under tables and ice machine;    and
D) KITCHEN - behind/under equipment, tables, and shelving throughout.

Clean the floors throughout daily/as needed, and maintain clean.

findings.comment:
750.800e - The following non-food contact surfaces were soiled with general buildup:
A) fryers - sides between fryers and side next to stove;
B) underneath wok line;
C) stove - 1. top & 2. drip tray;
D) inside oven beneath stove;
E) chest freezer - 1. outer surfaces (food splash) & 2. inside (ice/frost);   and
F) outer surfaces or bulk food storage bins (rice, salt & sugar).

Clean non-food contact surfaces daily/as needed to eliminate buildup of debris.
